
<%@page contentType="text/html" pageEncoding="UTF-8"%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
    <head>
        <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8">
        <title>MBA Program | The ICFAI University Shillong</title>
        <%@include file="common/headerfiles.jsp"%>
        <script>
            function bca1()
            {
                var data="";
                data="<span style='color:blue'>ABOUT THE PROGRAM</span><br>";
                data+="<p> The MBA Program of the University prepares the students with the knowledge, skills and strategic perspectives essential to business leadership and a managerial career in the world. The MBA Program is designed to provide both a portfolio of strong functional skills and the ability to apply, adapt and integrate those skills in different management settings. </p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Duration :</span><br>";
                data+="<p>Two years.</p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Eligibility :</span><br>";
                data+="<p> Graduation in any discipline with 45% and above aggregate marks. <br> Final year degree students awaiting results are also eligible to apply.</p>"
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Program Structure :</span><br>";
                data+="<p> The MBA Program is organized into 4 semesters in two years. There are 30 courses including soft skills. Students are additionally required to go through an internship and two management theses. </p>"
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Elective Streams</span><br>";
                data+="<p>The students are encouraged to choose eight courses from eight elective streams viz., Marketing, HRM, Finance, Banking, Investments, Insurance, Accounting and IT & Systems. Students will have the flexibility in choosing more than one course from these elective streams. Students will also have the facility for dual specialization. Elective courses will be offered subject to a minimum number of students enrolling for a particular elective course. </p>"
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Electives : </span><br>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Marketing : </span><br>";
                data+="<p> Integrated Marketing Communication, Services Marketing, International Marketing, Sales & Distribution Management, Marketing Research, B2B Marketing, Consumer Behavior, Retail Management, Strategic Marketing Management, Customer Relationship Management, Brand Management; </p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'> Banking : </span><br>";
                data+="<p> Money & Banking, Credit Management, Central Banking, Commercial Banking, Overview of Banking, Banking Services Operations, Rural Banking & Microfinance, Corporate Banking, Small and Medium Enterprises Banking;</p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'> Insurance : </span><br>";
                data+="<p> Life Insurance, General Insurance, Risk and Insurance, Claims Management, Underwriting Management</p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Finance :</span><br>";
                data+="<p> Strategic Financial Management, Security Analysis, Project Management, Management of Financial Institutions, Financial Risk Management; </p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'> HRM : </span><br>";
                data+="<p> Performance Management & Reward Systems, Training & Development, Leadership Skills & Change Management, Strategic HRM l Employment Laws, Managing Knowledge Workers, Corporate Communications, Human Resource Planning; </p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>IT & Systems:</span><br>";
                data+="<p> e-Business, Software Engineering & Quality Management, System Analysis & Design, Java Application Development, IT Enabled Services, Relational Database Management Systems, Data Warehousing, Data Mining; </p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Accounting : </span><br>";
                data+="<p>  Advanced Management Accounting, Advanced Financial Accounting;  </p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Investments : </span><br>";
                data+="<p>  Security Analysis, Portfolio Management and Mutual Funds, Personal Financial Planning, Wealth Management, Investment Banking and Financial Services. </p>";
                data+="<div style='padding:20px;'><table border='1' style='width:60%;border-collapse:collapse;'>";
                data+="<tr><td colspan='3'><center>MBA Program Structure</center></td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td style='padding:10px;'>Semester-I</td><td style='padding:10px;'>Semester-II</td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td style='padding:10px;'>YEAR I</td><td><ul><li>Marketing Management I</li>";
                data+="<li>Quantitative Methods</li><li>Financial Management 1</li><li>Organizational Behavior</li><li>Managerial Economics</li><li>Information Systems for Managers</li><li>Accounting for Managers</li><li>Business Communication</li></ul></td>";
                data+="<td><ul><li>Marketing Management II</li>";
                data+="<li>Financial Management II</li><li>Operations Management</li><li>Human Resource Management</li><li>Macro-Economics & Business Environment</li><li>Business Research Methods</li><li>Enterprise-wide Information Systems</li><li>Legal Environment of Business</li><li>Soft Skills Lab I</li></ul></td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td colspan='3'><center>Summer Internship</center></td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td style='padding:10px;'>Semester-III</td><td style='padding:10px;'>Semester-IV</td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td style='padding:10px;'>YEAR II</td><td><ul><li>Management Control Systems</li>";
                data+="<li>Business Strategy I</li><li>Elective I</li><li>Elective II</li><li>Elective III</li><li>Elective IV</li><li>Soft Skills Lab II</li><li>Management Thesis I</li></ul></td>";
                data+="<td><ul><li>Business Ethics & Corporate Governance</li>";
                data+="<li>Business Strategy II</li><li>Elective V</li><li>Elective VI</li><li>Elective VII</li><li>Elective VIII</li><li>Management Thesis II</li></ul></td></tr>";
                data+="</table></div><br>";
                document.getElementById("abouticfai").innerHTML=data;
            }
            function bca2()
            {
                var data="";
                data+="<span style='color:red;font-size:140%;'>ADMISSION MODALITIES</span><br><br>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Eligibility:</span><br>";
                data+="<ul><li>Pass in Graduation in any discipline from a recognized University with at least 45% marks. Final year degree students awaiting results are also eligible to apply.<br> For the purpose of determining eligibility based on aggregate percentage of marks, the procedure used by the respective university in award of the degree will only be taken into consideration. All applicants should have completed a minimum of 15 years of formal schooling by July 15, 2018. Applicants who have completed their graduation on a one-time sitting basis or on a 2-year basis are not eligible for admission to the MBA / M.Com / MTTM / IMCA Programs. <br> Students in their final year bachelor’s degree course are also eligible to apply, provided they complete their graduation requirements including practical examinations/viva assignments before July 15, 2018. Such applicants will have to produce a certificate to that effect at the time of admission. The admission of applicants will, however, remain provisional until they produce marksheets and a degree certificate establishing their eligibility. The registration of the candidates not meeting the criteria / non-submission of graduation transcripts by September 15, 2018. will be cancelled and admission fee will be forfeited and only 50% of the semester fee will be refunded after notifying the cancellation of the seat by the University. </li>";
                data+="<br><li>Students of Class XII who have not received the original certificates from the Board by July 15, 2018 will be admitted provisionally. Their admission will be confirmed subject to their passing the qualifying examination. The registration of the candidates not meeting the criteria by September 15, 2018 will be cancelled and admission fee will be forfeited and only 50% of the semester fee will be refunded after notifying the cancellation of the seat by the University.</li></ul>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Admission Criteria :</span><br>";
                data+="<ul><li> The selection of applicants into the Program is made through screening of applications and interview. While evaluating students for admission, due weightage is given to their academic distinction, awards in sports/cultural events, debates, quizzes and other extra cocurricular activities. </li>";
                data+="<br><li> Original certificates and Domicile certificate should be produced for verification at the time of payment of first semester fee. The original certificates will be returned after verification. </li></ul>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Special Reservation :</span><br>";
                data+="<ul><li> There shall be a special provision for admission of students belonging to the State of Meghalaya in any course of ICFAI University, Meghalaya, which shall not be less than 25 (twenty five) per cent of seats in each course / discipline subject to the students meeting the minimum qualifying requirements referred to above. </li>";
                data+="<br><li>  Seats remaining unfilled under special reservation may be filled up by allotting the same to students belonging to Open Category. </li></ul>";
                data+="<br><span style='color:red;font-size:140%;'>APPLICATION MODALITIES</span><br><br>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Guidelines on how to Complete the Application Form :</span><br>";
                data+="<p>The applicants are advised to read the guidelines carefully before completing the Application Form for Admission.</p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Application Form </span><br>";
                data+="<p>1.Please make sure that you meet the eligibility criteria before filling up the form.";
                data+="<br>2.Fill the Application Form in Capital Letters.<br>3.Provide all the available information under appropriate sections.";
                data+="<br>4.Make sure to sign the Application Form.<br>5.Retain a photocopy of the completed Application Form.";
                data+="<br>6.DD for Rs. 300.</p><br>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Attested Copies of Certificates :</span><br>";
                data+=" Applicants have to enclose attested copies of the following certificates (Attestation should be done by any Gazetted Officer/Principal of the College). ";
                data+="<ul><li> Date of Birth Certificate/Class X Certificate. </li><li> Marksheet of Class XII/Degree certificate (as may be applicable). </li>";
                data+="<li> Domicile Certificate. </li><li> Any other certificates pertaining to academic and other activities. </li><li> Please paste your recent passport size colour photograph on the Application Form given on next page. </li></ul><br>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Submission of Application Form :</span><br>";
                data+="<p> The completed Application Form for Admission along with a DD for Rs. 300 (drawn in favour of ‘The ICFAI University, Meghalaya - Fee Collection A/c’) may be submitted to:</p><br><br>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>The Admissions Officer,</span><br>";
                data+="<span style='color:gray'>The ICFAI University, Meghalaya,</span><br>";
                data+="<span style='color:gray'>Address :</span> Danakgre, (Near BSF Camp), P O Araimile,<br>";
                data+="<span style='color:gray'>Phone :</span> 9436716440<br>";
                data+="<span style='color:gray'>Shillong Campus:</span> Phawa Ville, Near Shillong Law College, Dhankheti,<br>";
                data+="<span style='color:gray'>Phone No: </span> 0364-2220057, 9485158603<br>";
                data+="<span style='color:gray'>E-mail:</span> admissions@iumeghalaya.edu.in<br>";
                data+="<span style='color:gray'>Website:</span> www.iumeghalaya.edu.in <br>";
                document.getElementById("abouticfai").innerHTML=data;
            }
            function bca3()
            {
                var data="";
                data+="<span style='color:red;font-size:140%;'>FEE SCHEDULE</span><br><br>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Fee :</span><br>";
                data+="<p> Admission Fee of Rs. 5,000 for UG Programs is to be paid by all the selected candidates immediately after the admission decision is announced. * Foreign students have to pay an admission fee of Rs. 6,000 for UG programs and Rs. 12,000 for PG Programs. The last date for payment of admission fee is June 29, 2018.</p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Program Fee :</span><br>";
                data+="<p> Students have to pay the program fee at the beginning of each semester, as per the due dates which will be indicated in the Student Handbook. The first semester fee is to be paid on or before July 10, 2018.</p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Domicile : </span><br>";
                data+="<p> Students from State of Meghalaya.</p>";
                data+="<span style='color:blue'>Non-Domicile :</span><br>";
                data+="<p> Students from States other than Meghalaya. </p>";
                data+="<div style='padding:20px;'><table border='1' style='width:60%;border-collapse:collapse;'>";
                data+="<tr><td rowspan='2'>Programs</td><td colspan='3'><center>Fee per semester (Rs.)</center></td><td colspan='3'><center>Total Program Fee (Rs.) </center></td></tr>"
                data+="<tr><td>Domicile</td><td>Non- Domicile</td><td>International</td><td>Domicile</td><td>Non- Domicile</td><td>International</td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td>MBA <br>(4 semesters)</td><td>48,500</td><td>59,500</td><td>75,000</td><td>1,94,000</td><td>2,38,000</td><td>3,00,000</td></tr>";
                data+="</table><br>";
                data+="<div style='padding:20px;'><table border='1' style='width:60%;border-collapse:collapse;'>";
                data+="<tr><td colspan='6'><center>Fee for Integrated Program</center></td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td colspan='2' rowspan='2'>Programs</td><td colspan='2'>Fee per semester (Rs.)</td><td colspan='2'>Total Program Fee (Rs.)</td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td>Domicile</td><td>Non-Domicile</td><td>Domicile</td><td>Non-Domicile</td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td rowspan='2'>IMCA</td><td>1 to 3 semesters</td><td>16,800</td><td>24,300</td><td rowspan='2'>2,60,400</td><td rowspan='2'>3,36,100</td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td>4 to 10 semesters</td><td>30,000</td><td>37,600</td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td rowspan='2'>IMCA (Foreign Students)*</td><td>1 to 5 semesters</td><td>-</td><td>58,620</td><td>-</td><td></td></tr>";
                data+="<tr><td>6 to 10 semesters</td><td>-</td><td>85,200</td><td>-</td><td>7,19,100</td></tr>";
                data+="</table>";
                data+="<br><p> All payments should be made by way of Demand Draft in favor of 'The ICFAI University, Meghalaya - Fee Collection A/c ' payable at Tura / Shillong, Meghalaya. </p>";
                document.getElementById("abouticfai").innerHTML=data;
            }
        </script>
    </head>
    <body onload="bca1()">
        <%@include file="common/header.jsp"%>
        <div id="bodycontent" style="padding-left:60px;min-height:2000px; padding-right:80px;">
            <br><br>
            <center>
                <table border="1px solid black;">
                    <button style="width:20%;min-height:10%;font-size:20px;" onclick="bca1();"">Program info</button>
                    <button style="width:20%;min-height:10%;font-size:20px;" onclick="bca2();">Admission</button>
                    <button style="width:20%;min-height:10%;font-size:20px;" onclick="bca3();">Fee Structure</button>
                </table>
            </center>
            <br>
            <div id="abouticfai" style="color:black;">
                
            </div>
        </div>
    </body>
</html>

